 Brackets\"}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"$L12\",\"/about\",{\"href\":\"/about\",\"className\":\"rounded-full border border-border/30 bg-card/30 px-3 py-1 text-muted-foreground hover:text-emerald-400 hover:border-emerald-500/30 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"About\"}]\n20:[\"$\",\"$L33\",null,{}]\n21:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.ssa.gov/oact/cola/cbb.html\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"SSA Contribution and Benefit Base\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 wage base: $184,500\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc751\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 751\"}],\" \",\"— Social Security and Medicare Withholding Rates\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc860\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 860\"}],\" \",\"— Additional Medicare Tax\"]}]]}]]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"State Income Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"State income tax calculations vary significantly by state. We provide dedicated income tax calculators for all 50 states, plus dedicated sales tax calculators for all 50 states as well. For states with progressive bracket systems (e.g., California, New York, Georgia), we apply each state’s published brackets to state taxable income. For flat-tax states (e.g., Illinois at 4.95%, Pennsylvania at 3.07%), we apply a single rate. For states with no individual income tax (e.g., Texas, Florida, Washington, Tennessee, Wyoming, Nevada, South Dakota, Alaska, New Hampshire), the state income tax component is zero. State standard deductions and personal exemptions are factored in where applicable. Our data is sourced directly from each state’s Department of Revenue or equivalent authority.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources (examples):\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.ftb.ca.gov/forms\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"California FTB\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 tax rate schedules and brackets\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.tax.ny.gov/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"NY Dept. of Taxation & Finance\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 income tax brackets\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://revenue.illinois.gov/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IL Dept. of Revenue\"}],\" \",\"— 4.95% flat rate and personal exemption\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://taxfoundation.org/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Tax Foundation\"}],\" \",\"— State Individual Income Tax Rates and Brackets (2026)\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"401(k) & Retirement Projections\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Our 401(k) calculator projects future retirement balances using compound growth with the formula: Balance = P × (1 + r)\",[\"$\",\"sup\",null,{\"children\":\"n\"}],\"+ C × [((1 + r)\",[\"$\",\"sup\",null,{\"children\":\"n\"}],\"− 1) / r], where P is the current balance, r is the assumed annual rate of return, n is the number of years, and C is the total annual contribution (employee + employer match). The 2026 401(k) contribution limit is $24,500 for those under 50, with an additional $8,000 catch-up contribution for those aged 50+, as set by the IRS. Employer match is applied according to the most common formula (50% match on the first 6% of salary). Projections are estimates only; actual returns will vary based on market conditions.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/401k-limit-increases-to-24500-for-2026-ira-limit-increases-to-7500\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS 401(k) Limit Announcement 2026\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 401(k) contribution limits: $24,500 / $32,500 (50+)\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/plan-participant-employee/retirement-topics-401k-and-profit-sharing-plan-contribution-limits\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Retirement Topics\"}],\" \",\"— 401(k) and profit sharing plan contribution limits\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Capital Gains Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Capital gains tax rates depend on the holding period and the taxpayer’s total taxable income. Short-term gains (assets held one year or less) are taxed as ordinary income using the federal brackets. Long-term gains (held more than one year) benefit from preferential rates: 0%, 15%, or 20%, depending on income level. For 2026, the 0% rate applies to taxable income up to $48,350 (single) or $96,700 (married filing jointly). The Net Investment Income Tax (NIIT) adds an additional 3.8% on investment income for individuals with modified AGI exceeding $200,000 (single) or $250,000 (MFJ). Our calculator factors in both the long-term rates and the NIIT surcharge.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc409\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 409\"}],\" \",\"— Capital Gains and Losses\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc559\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 559\"}],\" \",\"— Net Investment Income Tax\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Self-Employment Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Self-employment tax covers both the employer and employee portions of FICA for freelancers and independent contractors. The total rate is 15.3%: 12.4% for Social Security (on net earnings up to the $184,500 wage base) and 2.9% for Medicare (on all net earnings). However, only 92.35% of net self-employment income is subject to SE tax, and half of the total SE tax is deductible against ordinary income. Our calculator applies these rules exactly as specified in IRS Schedule SE and Publication 533.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-schedule-se-form-1040\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Schedule SE\"}],\" \",\"— Self-Employment Tax\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p533\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Publication 533\"}],\" \",\"— Self-Employment Tax\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Sales Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Our sales tax calculator uses combined rates that include the state base rate plus average local rates. For example, Texas has a 6.25% state sales tax but the average combined rate including local add-ons is approximately 8.2%. Five states (Oregon, Montana, Delaware, New Hampshire, Alaska) have no statewide sales tax, though Alaska and some others allow local sales taxes. Rates are sourced from each state’s revenue department and cross-referenced with the Tax Foundation’s annual state and local sales tax report.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://taxfoundation.org/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Tax Foundation\"}],\" \",\"— State and Local Sales Tax Rates, Midyear 2026\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc505\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 505\"}],\" \",\"— Deductible taxes (SALT deduction context)\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Property Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Property tax estimates are based on effective tax rates, calculated as the median annual property tax paid divided by the median home value in each state. These rates vary significantly: from approximately 0.28% in Hawaii to over 2.21% in New Jersey. Our data is drawn from the U.S. Census Bureau and Tax Foundation analyses. The calculator multiplies the home’s assessed value by the state’s average effective rate to produce an annual estimate. Actual property tax bills depend on local millage rates, assessment ratios, and exemptions (e.g., homestead exemptions in Florida), which vary by county.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://taxfoundation.org/data/all/state/property-taxes-by-state-county/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Tax Foundation\"}],\" \",\"— Property Taxes by State and County\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.census.gov/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"U.S. Census Bureau\"}],\" \",\"— Median home values and property tax data\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Payroll Deductions & Supplemental Income\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"For bonuses, overtime, and other supplemental wages, our calculators apply the IRS supplemental withholding rate of 22% for amounts under $1 million and 37% for amounts exceeding $1 million, as defined in IRS Publication 15-T. State supplemental rates are applied according to each state’s published rules. The lottery tax calculator applies the mandatory 24% federal withholding on winnings over $5,000, plus applicable state withholding, and then computes the actual tax liability at the taxpayer’s marginal rate (which may be higher than the withholding).\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p15t\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Publication 15-T\"}],\" \",\"— Supplemental wage withholding rates\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc419\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 419\"}],\" \",\"— Gambling income and withholding\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Privacy & Client-Side Computation\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"All tax calculations on TheTaxCalc.com are performed entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your income, deductions, and tax figures are never transmitted to our servers or stored in any database. The only data we collect is standard web analytics (page views, referral sources) and email addresses if you voluntarily subscribe to our newsletter. This architecture ensures that your sensitive financial information remains private and secure on your own device.\"}]]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Important Disclaimer\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"The calculations provided by TheTaxCalc.com are estimates for informational and educational purposes only. They do not constitute tax advice, and should not be used as the sole basis for financial decisions or tax filing. Individual tax situations vary based on many factors including but not limited to: additional deductions, credits, alternative minimum tax, foreign income, stock compensation, and multi-state filing obligations.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"We strongly recommend consulting a qualified tax professional (CPA, EA, or tax attorney) for advice specific to your situation. While we make every effort to ensure accuracy by sourcing data from official government publications, tax law changes frequently and errors may occur. Use of this tool constitutes acceptance of our\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L12\",null,{\"href\":\"/terms\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Terms of Use\"}],\".\"]}]]}]]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Update Schedule\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"We update our tax data on the following schedule to ensure accuracy:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Jan\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Annual IRS inflation adjustments and new bracket/rate data published\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Oct–Nov\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"SSA announces the upcoming year’s Social Security wage base\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Ongoing\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"State legislative changes incorporated within 30 days of enactment\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Quarterly\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Full review of all calculator logic and data sources for consistency\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$31\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@35\"}]}]\n2f:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n36:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/05-c3ty_6dwfk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/44p37290qsddb.js\"],\"IconMark\"]\n32:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Methodology: How TheTaxCalc Computes Your Taxes | TheTaxCalc\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Learn how TheTaxCalc computes federal, state, and FICA taxes for 2026. Every calculation is based on official IRS publications, SSA data, and state revenue department sources.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"author\",\"href\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"author\",\"content\":\"Rachel Mitchell, CPA\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"creator\",\"content\":\"TheTaxCalc\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"publisher\",\"content\":\"TheTaxCalc\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"googlebot\",\"content\":\"index, follow, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"category\",\"content\":\"finance\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"name\":\"classification\",\"content\":\"Tax Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"10\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"name\":\"google-site-verification\",\"content\":\"7bdac16b5ecbdd40\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Methodology: How TheTaxCalc Computes Taxes\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"How we compute your 2026 federal, state, and FICA taxes. All data sourced from IRS, SSA, and state revenue departments.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"property\":\"og:site_name\",\"content\":\"TheTaxCalc\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"website\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"TheTaxCalc — Free 2026 Paycheck & Mortgage Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"19\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Compute your take-home pay after federal, FICA, and state taxes. Supports IL, TX, FL, CA, NY.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"20\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/opengraph-image.png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"21\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"22\",{\"rel\":\"apple-touch-icon\",\"href\":\"/apple-touch-icon.png\"}],[\"$\",\"$L36\",\"23\",{}]]\n35:null\n","/methodology/__PAGE__":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/2g3ofza521d-d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3mzfoc5k_0lxh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/1h498-er8bjws.js\"],\"\"]\nf:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/05-c3ty_6dwfk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/44p37290qsddb.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n10:\"$Sreact.suspense\"\n0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground font-medium\",\"children\":\"Methodology\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"Methodology & Data Sources\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Every number on TheTaxCalc.com is derived from official government publications. This page documents exactly which sources we use, how each tax is calculated, and what assumptions go into our 2026 calculators.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-10\",\"children\":\"Last updated: January 2026 · Tax year: 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Federal Income Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Federal income tax is computed using the progressive bracket system defined in IRS Revenue Procedure 2025-25 and IRS Publication 15-T (Percentage Method Tables for Income Tax Withholding). For the 2026 tax year, there are seven brackets ranging from 10% to 37%. The standard deduction amounts are $16,100 for Single filers, $32,200 for Married Filing Jointly, and $24,150 for Head of Household. Our paycheck calculator applies these brackets sequentially to taxable income (gross income minus pre-tax deductions and the standard deduction), exactly as the IRS prescribes.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p15t\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Publication 15-T\"}],\" \",\"— Federal Income Tax Withholding Methods (2026)\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc551\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 551\"}],\" \",\"— Standard Deduction\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/filing/federal-income-tax-rates-and-brackets\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Revenue Procedure 2025-25\"}],\" \",\"— Annual inflation adjustments for 2026\"]}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"FICA: Social Security & Medicare\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"FICA taxes are calculated at 6.2% for Social Security (OASDI) on earnings up to the annual wage base limit, and 1.45% for Medicare (HI) on all earnings with no cap. For 2026, the Social Security wage base is $184,500, as announced by the Social Security Administration. An Additional Medicare Tax of 0.9% applies to earned income exceeding $200,000 for single filers ($250,000 for married filing jointly). Pre-tax deductions such as 401(k) contributions do not reduce FICA taxable income — only federal and state income tax. This is correctly reflected in all our calculators.\"}],\"$L3\"]}],\"$L4\",\"$L5\",\"$L6\",\"$L7\",\"$L8\",\"$L9\",\"$La\",\"$Lb\",\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\"]}],null,\"$Le\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"CoYzXiyUkcJG_1nbCXYOa\"}\n3:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.ssa.gov/oact/cola/cbb.html\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"SSA Contribution and Benefit Base\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 wage base: $184,500\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc751\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 751\"}],\" \",\"— Social Security and Medicare Withholding Rates\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc860\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 860\"}],\" \",\"— Additional Medicare Tax\"]}]]}]]}]\n4:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"State Income Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"State income tax calculations vary significantly by state. We provide dedicated income tax calculators for all 50 states, plus dedicated sales tax calculators for all 50 states as well. For states with progressive bracket systems (e.g., California, New York, Georgia), we apply each state’s published brackets to state taxable income. For flat-tax states (e.g., Illinois at 4.95%, Pennsylvania at 3.07%), we apply a single rate. For states with no individual income tax (e.g., Texas, Florida, Washington, Tennessee, Wyoming, Nevada, South Dakota, Alaska, New Hampshire), the state income tax component is zero. State standard deductions and personal exemptions are factored in where applicable. Our data is sourced directly from each state’s Department of Revenue or equivalent authority.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources (examples):\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.ftb.ca.gov/forms\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"California FTB\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 tax rate schedules and brackets\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.tax.ny.gov/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"NY Dept. of Taxation & Finance\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 income tax brackets\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://revenue.illinois.gov/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IL Dept. of Revenue\"}],\" \",\"— 4.95% flat rate and personal exemption\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://taxfoundation.org/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Tax Foundation\"}],\" \",\"— State Individual Income Tax Rates and Brackets (2026)\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n5:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"401(k) & Retirement Projections\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Our 401(k) calculator projects future retirement balances using compound growth with the formula: Balance = P × (1 + r)\",[\"$\",\"sup\",null,{\"children\":\"n\"}],\"+ C × [((1 + r)\",[\"$\",\"sup\",null,{\"children\":\"n\"}],\"− 1) / r], where P is the current balance, r is the assumed annual rate of return, n is the number of years, and C is the total annual contribution (employee + employer match). The 2026 401(k) contribution limit is $24,500 for those under 50, with an additional $8,000 catch-up contribution for those aged 50+, as set by the IRS. Employer match is applied according to the most common formula (50% match on the first 6% of salary). Projections are estimates only; actual returns will vary based on market conditions.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/401k-limit-increases-to-24500-for-2026-ira-limit-increases-to-7500\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS 401(k) Limit Announcement 2026\"}],\" \",\"— 2026 401(k) contribution limits: $24,500 / $32,500 (50+)\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/plan-participant-employee/retirement-topics-401k-and-profit-sharing-plan-contribution-limits\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Retirement Topics\"}],\" \",\"— 401(k) and profit sharing plan contribution limits\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Capital Gains Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Capital gains tax rates depend on the holding period and the taxpayer’s total taxable income. Short-term gains (assets held one year or less) are taxed as ordinary income using the federal brackets. Long-term gains (held more than one year) benefit from preferential rates: 0%, 15%, or 20%, depending on income level. For 2026, the 0% rate applies to taxable income up to $48,350 (single) or $96,700 (married filing jointly). The Net Investment Income Tax (NIIT) adds an additional 3.8% on investment income for individuals with modified AGI exceeding $200,000 (single) or $250,000 (MFJ). Our calculator factors in both the long-term rates and the NIIT surcharge.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc409\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 409\"}],\" \",\"— Capital Gains and Losses\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc559\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 559\"}],\" \",\"— Net Investment Income Tax\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Self-Employment Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Self-employment tax covers both the employer and employee portions of FICA for freelancers and independent contractors. The total rate is 15.3%: 12.4% for Social Security (on net earnings up to the $184,500 wage base) and 2.9% for Medicare (on all net earnings). However, only 92.35% of net self-employment income is subject to SE tax, and half of the total SE tax is deductible against ordinary income. Our calculator applies these rules exactly as specified in IRS Schedule SE and Publication 533.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-schedule-se-form-1040\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Schedule SE\"}],\" \",\"— Self-Employment Tax\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p533\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Publication 533\"}],\" \",\"— Self-Employment Tax\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n8:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Sales Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Our sales tax calculator uses combined rates that include the state base rate plus average local rates. For example, Texas has a 6.25% state sales tax but the average combined rate including local add-ons is approximately 8.2%. Five states (Oregon, Montana, Delaware, New Hampshire, Alaska) have no statewide sales tax, though Alaska and some others allow local sales taxes. Rates are sourced from each state’s revenue department and cross-referenced with the Tax Foundation’s annual state and local sales tax report.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://taxfoundation.org/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Tax Foundation\"}],\" \",\"— State and Local Sales Tax Rates, Midyear 2026\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc505\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 505\"}],\" \",\"— Deductible taxes (SALT deduction context)\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n9:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Property Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Property tax estimates are based on effective tax rates, calculated as the median annual property tax paid divided by the median home value in each state. These rates vary significantly: from approximately 0.28% in Hawaii to over 2.21% in New Jersey. Our data is drawn from the U.S. Census Bureau and Tax Foundation analyses. The calculator multiplies the home’s assessed value by the state’s average effective rate to produce an annual estimate. Actual property tax bills depend on local millage rates, assessment ratios, and exemptions (e.g., homestead exemptions in Florida), which vary by county.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://taxfoundation.org/data/all/state/property-taxes-by-state-county/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Tax Foundation\"}],\" \",\"— Property Taxes by State and County\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.census.gov/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"U.S. Census Bureau\"}],\" \",\"— Median home values and property tax data\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\na:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Payroll Deductions & Supplemental Income\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"For bonuses, overtime, and other supplemental wages, our calculators apply the IRS supplemental withholding rate of 22% for amounts under $1 million and 37% for amounts exceeding $1 million, as defined in IRS Publication 15-T. State supplemental rates are applied according to each state’s published rules. The lottery tax calculator applies the mandatory 24% federal withholding on winnings over $5,000, plus applicable state withholding, and then computes the actual tax liability at the taxpayer’s marginal rate (which may be higher than the withholding).\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Primary Sources:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p15t\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Publication 15-T\"}],\" \",\"— Supplemental wage withholding rates\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc419\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"IRS Topic No. 419\"}],\" \",\"— Gambling income and withholding\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Privacy & Client-Side Computation\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"All tax calculations on TheTaxCalc.com are performed entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your income, deductions, and tax figures are never transmitted to our servers or stored in any database. The only data we collect is standard web analytics (page views, referral sources) and email addresses if you voluntarily subscribe to our newsletter. This architecture ensures that your sensitive financial information remains private and secure on your own device.\"}]]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Important Disclaimer\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"The calculations provided by TheTaxCalc.com are estimates for informational and educational purposes only. They do not constitute tax advice, and should not be used as the sole basis for financial decisions or tax filing. Individual tax situations vary based on many factors including but not limited to: additional deductions, credits, alternative minimum tax, foreign income, stock compensation, and multi-state filing obligations.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"We strongly recommend consulting a qualified tax professional (CPA, EA, or tax attorney) for advice specific to your situation. While we make every effort to ensure accuracy by sourcing data from official government publications, tax law changes frequently and errors may occur. Use of this tool constitutes acceptance of our\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/terms\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"Terms of Use\"}],\".\"]}]]}]]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Update Schedule\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"We update our tax data on the following schedule to ensure accuracy:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Jan\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Annual IRS inflation adjustments and new bracket/rate data published\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Oct–Nov\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"SSA announces the upcoming year’s Social Security wage base\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Ongoing\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"State legislative changes incorporated within 30 days of enactment\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"flex gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0\",\"children\":\"Quarterly\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Full review of all calculator logic and data sources for consistency\"}]]}]]}]]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$10\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@11\"}]}]\n11:null\n","/methodology":"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[39756,[\"/_next/static/chunks/05-c3ty_6dwfk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/44p37290qsddb.js\"],\"default\"]\n3:I[37457,[\"/_next/static/chunks/05-c3ty_6dwfk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/44p37290qsddb.js\"],\"default\"]\n4:[]\n0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}]}]]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":\"$W4\",\"buildId\":\"CoYzXiyU